WEBVTT

00:56.556 --> 01:00.977
LOVE NEXT DOOR

01:13.615 --> 01:16.910
Just wait, my baby.
I'll make it look nice for you.

01:30.048 --> 01:32.300
What am I going to do now?

01:33.593 --> 01:36.638
Don't worry. It'll be all gone
when you wake up tomorrow.

01:36.721 --> 01:38.932
What if it's not gone?

01:39.015 --> 01:40.725
Then…

01:43.269 --> 01:44.312
I'll take responsibility.

01:45.146 --> 01:48.399
I, Bae Seok-ryu, will take responsibility
for you, Choi Seung-hyo.

01:48.483 --> 01:49.359
I promise.

01:50.777 --> 01:51.903
Seal it.

01:54.948 --> 01:56.741
Good. Great job.

01:56.825 --> 01:59.536
PUPPY LOVE

01:59.619 --> 02:00.995
Okay. Let's eat this.

02:11.756 --> 02:14.592
I said I didn't need the banana milk.
Why did you buy it?

02:14.676 --> 02:16.469
That was that, and this is this.

02:17.220 --> 02:18.179
What?

02:18.847 --> 02:23.726
What is "that"?
What do you mean by "that was that"?

02:23.810 --> 02:25.603
What do you think? It's "that."

02:25.687 --> 02:28.231
In English, it's called "that."
It's a demonstrative pronoun.

02:28.314 --> 02:30.692
Yeah, I know. That's what that is.

02:30.775 --> 02:33.194
But what I meant… was that…

02:34.237 --> 02:35.321
Jeez.

02:35.822 --> 02:37.407
This word's losing all meaning.

02:39.826 --> 02:40.994
Hey.

02:41.077 --> 02:42.162
What?

02:43.037 --> 02:44.247
What are we now?

02:44.914 --> 02:46.040
I don't know.

02:47.417 --> 02:49.294
Whatever a relationship after a kiss is?

02:49.377 --> 02:50.211
Hey!

02:50.837 --> 02:52.380
That kiss…

02:52.463 --> 02:55.133
Can you not say that word
so suddenly like that?

02:56.593 --> 02:58.094
I don't kiss my friends.

02:58.177 --> 03:00.763
I said stop doing that!

03:01.389 --> 03:02.891
We're not kissing now. We did before.

03:02.974 --> 03:04.183
No, what I meant was…

03:04.267 --> 03:07.353
Stop saying that word itself.

03:07.437 --> 03:09.981
-The word? Kiss?
-Stop!

03:13.067 --> 03:16.613
Also, I don't do that
with my friends either.

03:17.530 --> 03:18.656
Then, it's settled.

03:19.699 --> 03:21.034
We're not friends anymore.

03:22.785 --> 03:26.122
How can 30 years of friendship
end just like that?

03:27.290 --> 03:29.542
It was the hardest thing
I've done in my life.

03:30.585 --> 03:33.046
Winning an Olympic medal
would've been easier.

03:36.424 --> 03:37.675
Seung-hyo! Seok-ryu!

03:39.052 --> 03:41.346
-Mr. Yoon.
-What? You two already met up?

03:41.429 --> 03:42.931
You were looking frantically for him.

03:43.014 --> 03:45.016
I thought he owed you money
or something.

03:45.099 --> 03:46.267
-Really?
-Yeah.

03:46.351 --> 03:50.605
Goodness, Mr. Yoon!
When did I ever act like that?

03:50.688 --> 03:52.190
-You did…
-Jeez.

03:52.273 --> 03:54.484
Then, why did you come here?

03:54.567 --> 03:58.363
I mean, why would you come
all the way from Seoul to see him?

03:58.446 --> 04:00.114
-Well, actually--
-Hey!

04:00.198 --> 04:01.824
-Hold on!
-You scared me.

04:01.908 --> 04:04.369
Do you really think
I came here to see him?

04:04.452 --> 04:08.122
I just came and was in the area,
so I thought I'd call him.

04:08.206 --> 04:09.832
Right.

04:09.916 --> 04:12.168
Yeah, so why did you come?

04:12.252 --> 04:14.921
I just came here!

04:15.004 --> 04:17.006
I just came here, so I called him.

04:17.090 --> 04:18.508
Okay, great.

04:18.591 --> 04:21.511
But it's still a pretty far drive.
So what brings you here?

04:21.594 --> 04:23.721
No, I'm telling you it's personal!

04:23.805 --> 04:26.891
It's personal, so why do they keep asking?

04:27.433 --> 04:30.228
-I didn't take him for the type.
-Wait, are you crying?

04:30.311 --> 04:32.730
Did I do something wrong?

04:32.814 --> 04:34.399
-I feel like I was scolded.
-Is she mad?

04:37.402 --> 04:40.530
This is what I believe.

04:41.072 --> 04:43.241
If you're someone who cooks,

04:43.324 --> 04:45.660
you have to try food
from Gangwon Province,

04:45.743 --> 04:48.705
which subtly enhances
the original taste of the ingredients.

04:50.456 --> 04:53.376
So you came all the way here to eat?

04:53.459 --> 04:55.878
See? I knew you wouldn't believe me,

04:55.962 --> 04:58.548
so I wasn't going to tell you.

04:59.340 --> 05:00.550
It's true.

05:00.633 --> 05:03.094
This gajami sikhae
is especially good. Seriously.

05:03.177 --> 05:05.179
Gajami sikhae? What?

05:05.263 --> 05:06.889
They made sikhye with fish? No way.

05:06.973 --> 05:08.766
It's red too. I can't eat spicy food.

05:08.850 --> 05:10.435
-It's not what you think.
-What?

05:10.518 --> 05:12.603
It sounds like sikhye,
but it's not the drink.

05:12.687 --> 05:14.147
-It's spelled differently.
-Is it?

05:14.230 --> 05:15.315
-It's flounder.
-Okay.

05:15.398 --> 05:17.233
They add rice and salt to it
and ferment it.

05:17.317 --> 05:19.319
-That's how the dish is made.
-Fermented?

05:19.402 --> 05:22.864
He's messing with you.
He loves fermented fish dishes.

05:22.947 --> 05:24.240
What?

05:24.324 --> 05:25.950
You're a total food connoisseur!

05:26.034 --> 05:28.369
Well, I wouldn't say "connoisseur."

05:28.453 --> 05:31.039
He's marked
over 100 restaurants on the Greip map.

05:31.122 --> 05:33.541
No, it was 328 as of yesterday.

05:35.001 --> 05:36.419
Can you share those with me?

05:36.502 --> 05:37.420
No way!

05:37.503 --> 05:39.547
I'm going to hand them down to my twins.

05:40.631 --> 05:41.466
-Please!
-Still…

05:41.549 --> 05:43.551
You've helped us out a lot.

05:43.634 --> 05:45.470
So I'll give them all to you.

05:46.220 --> 05:48.264
Thank you! This meal is on me then.

05:48.347 --> 05:50.099
Thank you! Let's eat!

05:50.183 --> 05:52.185
I bet you're hungry. Eat this.

05:58.983 --> 05:59.942
Me.

06:00.526 --> 06:02.487
You like marinated raw crabs, right?

06:02.570 --> 06:04.155
-Eat this.
-I do?

06:05.073 --> 06:07.116
No? What about Na-yun?
What did you like?

06:07.200 --> 06:09.327
You. I like you.

06:09.410 --> 06:10.953
Okay, you can eat whatever you like.

06:11.037 --> 06:13.539
I want to eat that. It looks so good.

06:14.290 --> 06:15.291
Eat up.

06:15.374 --> 06:16.209
Okay.

06:21.714 --> 06:23.549
The gajami sikhae has great texture.

06:24.842 --> 06:26.886
I could absolutely destroy it.

06:30.932 --> 06:31.891
-Eat up.
-Okay.

06:45.738 --> 06:46.906
Yes?

06:46.989 --> 06:47.949
Can I come in?

06:48.032 --> 06:48.991
Sure.

06:50.284 --> 06:52.995
Hey, is it really okay to stay here?

06:53.079 --> 06:55.581
Seriously, I can find another place.

06:55.665 --> 06:57.375
There are plenty of empty rooms.

06:58.251 --> 06:59.293
Also, here.

06:59.377 --> 07:01.295
I thought you'd need more clothes.

07:01.379 --> 07:02.964
Right, thanks.

07:03.047 --> 07:05.424
Gosh, I've been borrowing clothes
a lot lately.

07:07.301 --> 07:09.762
The bathroom's at the end
of the hall, so you can wash up.

07:09.846 --> 07:10.888
Okay, I got it.

07:18.187 --> 07:19.355
Were there any bugs?

07:19.439 --> 07:21.149
-No.
-Okay.

07:27.155 --> 07:28.489
-You're not leaving?
-What?

07:28.573 --> 07:29.824
Aren't you going to go?

07:29.907 --> 07:32.452
-Just for a moment--
-Seung-hyo!

07:32.535 --> 07:34.287
Seung-hyo, where are you?

07:35.955 --> 07:37.623
Go on. She's looking for you.

07:37.707 --> 07:39.542
Are you sure you want me to go?

07:40.251 --> 07:41.085
What?

07:41.169 --> 07:43.337
Back then and now.

07:44.005 --> 07:45.631
Why do you keep giving me dirty looks?

07:45.715 --> 07:46.799
What are you talking about?

07:46.883 --> 07:48.718
My gaze is so gentle right now.

07:48.801 --> 07:51.179
You should look in the mirror
when you say that.

07:52.138 --> 07:53.723
Wait a second.

07:55.725 --> 07:57.018
Are you jealous?

07:57.977 --> 08:00.438
Don't be ridiculous. Hurry and get out.

08:00.521 --> 08:01.522
Stop laughing. Go.

08:01.606 --> 08:03.649
Fine, I'm leaving. Why are you pushing?

08:03.733 --> 08:04.942
Just go.

08:21.751 --> 08:22.793
Seung-hyo.

08:23.377 --> 08:24.212
What?

08:24.712 --> 08:26.589
My wife's not here, so I can't sleep.

08:47.527 --> 08:48.945
-Are you asleep?
-No.

08:53.241 --> 08:54.325
Want to come out for a bit?

08:54.408 --> 08:55.743
Yard in 10 minutes. By the tree.

09:08.422 --> 09:10.132
It's late. Why weren't you asleep?

09:10.216 --> 09:11.217
What about you?

09:12.218 --> 09:14.303
I was reading.

09:15.388 --> 09:18.891
Mokminsimseo?
The book Jeong Yak-yong wrote?

09:19.475 --> 09:20.309
Yeah.

09:20.393 --> 09:22.895
Who reads those kinds of books these days?

09:23.396 --> 09:24.230
I do.

09:25.398 --> 09:28.401
It's been a classic since long ago
that transcends time.

09:29.610 --> 09:33.239
It teaches integrity, responsibility,
and how to lead by example.

09:33.322 --> 09:35.491
It tells you how to live.

09:35.575 --> 09:37.827
This book provides enlightenment
about life.

09:37.910 --> 09:40.496
Okay, don't get worked up.

09:40.580 --> 09:42.498
Did I get worked up?

09:42.582 --> 09:45.167
Well, it just seemed like
you didn't know the value of this book.

09:46.544 --> 09:48.713
By the way, it's really nice here.

09:50.131 --> 09:52.216
It's too bad I'm only staying for a day.

09:52.758 --> 09:54.594
You can come again next time.

09:55.886 --> 09:57.138
I'll go back with you tomorrow.

09:57.597 --> 09:58.681
What about your work?

09:58.764 --> 10:00.474
I finished earlier than expected.

10:01.434 --> 10:05.521
I was going to leave the day
after tomorrow, but I can go a day early.

10:06.272 --> 10:07.273
Let's go together.

10:07.815 --> 10:10.067
How? You drove here.

10:10.151 --> 10:11.944
I need to drive Mo-eum's car back.

10:13.195 --> 10:14.196
For my car…

10:15.364 --> 10:17.450
-I'll call a designated driver.
-Are you insane?

10:17.533 --> 10:20.661
Do you know how expensive that would be?

10:21.287 --> 10:23.956
Yeah, that does sound crazy to me too.

10:25.541 --> 10:26.792
But when I thought about it,

10:26.876 --> 10:29.086
I realized spending time with you
was worth more.

10:29.170 --> 10:31.505
Please. You've got to be kidding me.

10:31.589 --> 10:34.884
You like me that much?

10:36.427 --> 10:37.970
-Yeah.
-I see.

10:40.598 --> 10:43.142
Well, how much do you like me?

10:44.894 --> 10:47.688
Even after 30 years together,
I'm still not sick of you.

10:47.772 --> 10:49.774
Wow, that's a bit of an exaggeration.

10:51.025 --> 10:53.319
Have some shame
and take out the times we were apart.

10:54.528 --> 10:55.905
But there weren't any.

10:58.240 --> 11:00.785
I've always been with you.

11:08.250 --> 11:09.085
Here.

11:11.128 --> 11:12.254
When we were eight,

11:12.338 --> 11:15.800
you splashed paint all over me.

11:22.723 --> 11:23.891
When we were seven,

11:25.267 --> 11:28.646
you put sticker tattoos
on my face while I was asleep.

11:35.236 --> 11:36.195
When we were six,

11:38.280 --> 11:39.990
you gave me magic candy

11:40.783 --> 11:43.661
that turned my lips purple
so you could tease me.

11:57.174 --> 12:00.010
And when we were five,
I spat bubble gum on your hair.

12:00.511 --> 12:01.429
Jeez.

12:05.266 --> 12:10.062
Wow, how could you still like me
after enduring all that suffering?

12:11.897 --> 12:12.731
See?

12:12.815 --> 12:15.317
I told you I was a femme fatale.

12:15.901 --> 12:18.237
-Get off me.
-No.

12:19.488 --> 12:21.824
You said we've always
been together like this.

12:26.620 --> 12:28.914
I'm a bit sleepy now though.

12:29.957 --> 12:31.000
You are?

12:31.917 --> 12:33.419
Yeah.

12:33.502 --> 12:35.421
Maybe it's because of that long drive.

12:39.925 --> 12:42.344
We can't have someone
come out and see us though.

13:30.226 --> 13:31.060
Ms. Jung Mo-eum?

13:31.936 --> 13:32.937
Yes.

13:38.692 --> 13:39.568
INTERVIEW ROOM

13:39.693 --> 13:44.949
INTERVIEW FOR SOUTH POLE
RESEARCH STATION PARAMEDIC POSITION

13:45.533 --> 13:46.742
Ms. Jung Mo-eum.

13:47.701 --> 13:51.205
You have a high TOEIC score
and a recreational watercraft license.

13:51.288 --> 13:53.499
You're also a certified Level 1 paramedic.

13:54.708 --> 13:56.252
You're well-prepared.

13:56.335 --> 13:59.797
Yes, sir. Not only did I do my best
to excel in fire safety management,

13:59.880 --> 14:02.466
but I also worked hard
to perform my duties in the field.

14:03.759 --> 14:05.344
Why do you want to go to Antarctica?

14:05.427 --> 14:09.640
To be honest, my dream
was to become Superman when I was a kid.

14:11.267 --> 14:13.185
Then, I wanted to be Spider-Man.

14:14.853 --> 14:17.815
I realized I couldn't be either,
so I joined the Korea Fire Service.

14:18.691 --> 14:21.110
And I've been very satisfied with my job.

14:23.571 --> 14:25.614
Because I'm still able to help people.

14:27.324 --> 14:28.951
Yes, I guess you're right.

14:29.034 --> 14:32.454
I'd like to go to Antarctica
to experience an unknown world

14:32.538 --> 14:34.498
and to help preserve world peace.

14:36.041 --> 14:38.294
MINISTRY OF FOREIGN AFFAIRS

15:02.943 --> 15:06.238
Thank you for telling me
about Hye-suk last time.

15:06.322 --> 15:07.948
I'm glad she's safe.

15:08.032 --> 15:09.575
But…

15:09.658 --> 15:12.786
this is as far as my gratitude
for Hye-suk will go.

15:13.662 --> 15:16.916
-Excuse me?
-Seo Hye-suk is my wife.

15:16.999 --> 15:17.917
She's my woman.

15:20.920 --> 15:21.837
I know that.

15:21.921 --> 15:23.881
Then, that's more reason
to not behave like this.

15:24.465 --> 15:26.091
Don't try to sway her anymore.

15:26.175 --> 15:28.594
I think there's a misunderstanding.

15:28.677 --> 15:31.347
I heard your nickname is Alain Delon.

15:31.430 --> 15:32.973
Why suddenly bring that up?

15:33.057 --> 15:37.436
-Yes, you're handsome.
-Excuse me, Dr. Choi.

15:37.519 --> 15:40.272
However, my feelings for her won't change.

15:40.356 --> 15:42.274
The reason for that is

15:42.358 --> 15:43.567
I love Hye-suk!

15:44.151 --> 15:44.985
Darling.

15:47.613 --> 15:48.697
What's going on?

15:53.410 --> 15:55.871
What are you doing here? Well?

15:55.955 --> 15:57.122
Well…

15:57.206 --> 16:00.125
Hye-suk and I are just friends.

16:00.209 --> 16:02.378
She just called you "Darling"!

16:02.461 --> 16:04.463
What kind of friends call each other that?

16:04.546 --> 16:07.716
-We do, because we're close.
-We're really just friends.

16:07.800 --> 16:10.177
I've never once harbored
feelings for her.

16:10.260 --> 16:11.804
That's why it's so ridiculous!

16:11.887 --> 16:14.348
She's such a beautiful
and intelligent woman.

16:15.224 --> 16:17.267
How could you not fall for her?

16:17.351 --> 16:18.560
Are you a robot?

16:23.148 --> 16:24.733
I'm gay.

16:24.817 --> 16:26.694
-Gosh.
-Excuse me?

16:26.777 --> 16:30.072
I like men.

16:41.500 --> 16:44.044
You're such a beautiful
and intelligent woman.

16:44.128 --> 16:46.505
Stop it. Jeez.

16:47.381 --> 16:50.134
I'm sorry. I'm so embarrassed.

16:50.217 --> 16:51.343
Don't be sorry.

16:51.427 --> 16:53.137
It was actually nice.

16:53.971 --> 16:56.598
He can declare his love for you
with such confidence.

16:56.682 --> 16:59.727
Gosh, he's such a fool.

16:59.810 --> 17:02.354
Seeing that made me envious.

17:02.438 --> 17:04.732
What's there to be envious about?

17:06.233 --> 17:08.819
I'm pretty old now too.

17:10.029 --> 17:12.364
Maybe I should be braver as well.

17:14.742 --> 17:16.910
Whatever you choose to do,
I'll support you.

17:17.453 --> 17:18.328
You know that, right?

17:19.621 --> 17:25.544
I know. Always and forever.

17:52.279 --> 17:54.656
I'm so embarrassed by you right now.

17:55.157 --> 17:56.784
-Stay two steps behind me.
-Okay.

18:00.913 --> 18:02.748
I mean, how could you…

18:05.292 --> 18:08.420
-How could you doubt me?
-I didn't doubt you. That bastard…

18:08.504 --> 18:11.340
I mean, I was afraid
he might've had bad intentions.

18:11.423 --> 18:13.884
Regardless of the reason, I'm sorry.

18:13.967 --> 18:14.843
Unbelievable.

18:18.305 --> 18:21.892
Why didn't you tell me sooner?
I wouldn't have misunderstood if you did.

18:21.975 --> 18:25.145
My friend trusted me with that secret.
How could I tell you?

18:25.229 --> 18:28.357
He must've been so uneasy living
in this conservative and rigid society.

18:31.235 --> 18:34.071
That's so cool. You're so cool.

18:35.280 --> 18:36.115
Jeez.

18:37.491 --> 18:39.451
-What are you doing? Let's go.
-Coming.

18:44.581 --> 18:46.291
Gosh, I'm so embarrassed.

18:47.459 --> 18:49.128
That was so embarrassing.

18:49.211 --> 18:51.463
Goodness. What do you think you're doing?

18:51.964 --> 18:53.799
SEND YOUR NAME,
ADDRESS, PHONE NUMBER

18:53.882 --> 18:55.384
ORDERS WILL BE PROCESSED UPON PAYMENT

18:58.178 --> 19:02.391
Yeah! I did it!

19:02.474 --> 19:05.310
You scared me. What are you yelling for?

19:05.394 --> 19:07.104
Mom, are you ready?

19:07.187 --> 19:09.148
Yeah, the food's ready. Help yourself.

19:09.231 --> 19:12.317
No, not food.
Are you ready for the good life?

19:12.401 --> 19:14.403
-You know the money you lent me?
-Yeah?

19:14.486 --> 19:16.196
I'll multiply it by a hundred. A thousand!

19:16.280 --> 19:18.740
Are you an influenza now?

19:18.824 --> 19:20.701
No, not influenza. An influencer.

19:20.784 --> 19:22.035
Right, influencer.

19:22.119 --> 19:24.913
No, wait. Like a virus,
I'm going to be deadly.

19:24.997 --> 19:26.623
And I'll become more infectious.

19:26.707 --> 19:28.208
Just try to break even.

19:28.876 --> 19:32.296
Mom, trust your son!
It's for real this time.

19:32.379 --> 19:34.882
Also, don't carry around
things like this anymore.

19:34.965 --> 19:36.466
-Let's throw it out.
-Hey!

19:36.550 --> 19:39.219
Why would I toss out a perfectly fine bag?

19:40.637 --> 19:42.181
Mom, this won't do.

19:43.098 --> 19:45.434
Have a bag picked out.

19:45.517 --> 19:46.768
I'll buy it for you soon.

19:46.852 --> 19:49.605
Even if I had a bag like that,
I have nowhere to bring it to.

19:49.688 --> 19:52.524
All I want is for you to be a success.

19:53.775 --> 19:54.651
That's all.

19:56.778 --> 19:57.779
Bye.

19:58.947 --> 20:01.533
Mom, go to the mall. Okay?

20:02.451 --> 20:03.285
Pick one out!

20:03.368 --> 20:05.120
-In-suk, eat this first.
-Okay.

20:07.331 --> 20:08.332
-Hey.
-What?

20:08.415 --> 20:12.044
How much does
a designer bag cost these days?

20:12.878 --> 20:14.796
-Prices vary greatly.
-Right.

20:14.880 --> 20:16.882
But they're at least
two to three million won.

20:16.965 --> 20:18.175
Goodness, that's insane.

20:18.258 --> 20:21.220
With that kind of money,
you could buy 30 kg of Hanwoo!

20:21.303 --> 20:22.471
Gosh, that's expensive.

20:22.554 --> 20:24.014
But why do you suddenly ask?

20:25.140 --> 20:26.558
Is Geun-sik buying you one?

20:26.642 --> 20:30.520
It'd be faster to be reborn than
to expect something like that from him.

20:32.147 --> 20:34.191
No, Dong-jin…

20:34.274 --> 20:35.734
Never mind. Later.

20:35.817 --> 20:37.736
-What?
-No, it's nothing.

20:37.819 --> 20:39.196
It's just…

20:39.905 --> 20:41.114
-Hey, Mi-suk.
-Yeah?

20:41.198 --> 20:43.992
I don't know
if it's right to ask you this or not,

20:44.701 --> 20:46.411
but it's about Seok-ryu.

20:47.120 --> 20:48.747
Would she be interested in a blind date?

20:50.624 --> 20:51.458
A blind date?

20:55.587 --> 20:57.547
Why is the dog barking so much?

20:59.258 --> 21:01.134
Don't you think you were a bit harsh?

21:01.635 --> 21:02.469
About what?

21:02.552 --> 21:05.889
How could you drive all the way back
without stopping at a rest area?

21:05.973 --> 21:07.975
Did you want to go to the bathroom?

21:08.058 --> 21:11.645
It's not that.
It was supposed to be a date.

21:11.728 --> 21:13.355
I should've just driven my car.

21:13.981 --> 21:15.816
I need to give Mo-eum her car back.

21:15.899 --> 21:17.651
I told you
we should drive back separately.

21:17.734 --> 21:18.610
-Seok-ryu!
-But…

21:19.361 --> 21:20.487
-Mom.
-Hey, Seung-hyo.

21:20.570 --> 21:21.989
-Aunt Mi-suk.
-Why are you…

21:22.072 --> 21:24.157
Mom, the reason why we're together is--

21:24.241 --> 21:26.743
No, I was just about to call you.

21:26.827 --> 21:28.787
Do you want to go on a blind date?

21:28.870 --> 21:29.705
A blind date?

21:29.788 --> 21:31.415
Goodness! Why are you the one surprised?

21:31.498 --> 21:33.458
Jeez, Mom. Don't be ridiculous.

21:33.542 --> 21:37.045
Your Aunt Jae-suk wants to
set you up with someone.

21:37.838 --> 21:40.257
I'm not forcing you either,
but he seems decent.

21:40.340 --> 21:41.216
No, she can't.

21:41.300 --> 21:43.719
She's in no position to do that.

21:43.802 --> 21:45.887
-Mom! Let's talk at home.
-No, not later. Now!

21:45.971 --> 21:47.514
I have to tell her quick.

21:47.597 --> 21:50.267
Jae-suk wants to introduce him to Mo-eum,

21:50.350 --> 21:51.768
but she won't listen.

21:51.852 --> 21:52.686
Me?

21:52.769 --> 21:53.979
There's that disobedient girl.

21:56.189 --> 21:57.607
Give me an answer now.

21:57.691 --> 21:58.608
What?

22:00.986 --> 22:02.446
Wow.

22:02.529 --> 22:06.366
I was busy eating that night
I didn't look around properly.

22:06.450 --> 22:10.370
Goodness. Company benefits are good here.

22:10.454 --> 22:12.372
There's a massage chair too.

22:12.956 --> 22:16.168
Yeah, we're trying our best.

22:16.251 --> 22:17.377
Right.

22:18.795 --> 22:22.174
Even the massage chair
is different at an architecture firm.

22:22.257 --> 22:23.342
It's so pretty.

22:27.679 --> 22:30.682
All right, then.
How about we hear the report now?

22:30.766 --> 22:32.392
-What report?
-Come on.

22:34.436 --> 22:36.688
My car came back today,

22:36.772 --> 22:39.649
which means Seok-ryu spent the night out.

22:41.276 --> 22:42.110
Are you two…

22:43.612 --> 22:45.197
dating now?

22:45.280 --> 22:47.115
I did spend the night out,

22:47.199 --> 22:49.826
but it's definitely not
what you're thinking.

22:49.910 --> 22:52.037
Yeah, we were at our lodgings.

22:52.120 --> 22:54.414
We slept separately in separate rooms.

22:54.498 --> 22:56.833
Yeah, sure. Let's say that happened.

22:57.459 --> 22:59.795
But why won't you answer my question?

23:00.378 --> 23:01.338
What?

23:01.421 --> 23:02.756
Are you two dating?

23:06.718 --> 23:07.969
Yeah, we are.

23:12.307 --> 23:14.434
Finally! At long last!

23:15.268 --> 23:16.436
I feel so refreshed.

23:16.520 --> 23:18.563
Seriously, you two!

23:20.273 --> 23:23.610
This feels like my body
and soul's been massaged!

23:23.693 --> 23:25.320
Gosh, this feels good!

23:26.488 --> 23:29.866
Why are you so happy about us dating?

23:29.950 --> 23:32.869
Because I almost died of frustration.

23:32.953 --> 23:36.373
I bet everyone who's watched you two
feels the same way.

23:36.873 --> 23:40.752
However, I knew you two
would end up together.

23:40.836 --> 23:43.797
Hey, how would you know
something even we didn't know?

23:44.548 --> 23:46.508
There's power in words.

23:56.434 --> 24:02.357
Seung-hyo and Seok-ryu sitting in a tree

24:02.440 --> 24:06.444
K-I-S-S-I-N-G

24:06.528 --> 24:07.487
First comes love

24:07.571 --> 24:09.573
You're all dead!

24:10.240 --> 24:14.119
Then comes marriage

24:14.202 --> 24:17.706
Then comes baby in a baby carriage

24:17.789 --> 24:20.208
Seung-hyo and Seok-ryu

24:20.292 --> 24:21.668
Get back here!

24:21.751 --> 24:22.961
Sitting in a tree

24:31.136 --> 24:33.972
Hey, why do you two
always go home together?

24:34.055 --> 24:35.682
We live next door.

24:35.765 --> 24:38.310
Still, boys and girls
shouldn't hang out with each other.

24:39.186 --> 24:42.063
Seung-hyo and Seok-ryu sitting in a tree

24:42.147 --> 24:46.151
K-I-S-S-I-N-G

24:46.234 --> 24:49.654
That's not true! He's just my sidekick!

24:49.738 --> 24:53.116
First comes love

24:53.200 --> 24:55.202
Then comes marriage

24:55.285 --> 24:58.496
Then comes baby in a baby carriage

24:58.580 --> 25:00.040
Seung-hyo and Seok-ryu

25:00.123 --> 25:02.876
Hey, Choisseung.
Give me your history textbook.

25:03.877 --> 25:05.045
What am I, the library?

25:06.046 --> 25:07.505
Hey, what's with you two?

25:07.589 --> 25:08.965
-Are you two dating?
-Nope.

25:09.049 --> 25:11.134
Seeing him naked wouldn't faze me at all.

25:11.218 --> 25:13.011
Just think of her as a guy.

25:13.094 --> 25:14.512
Hey, you two.

25:17.682 --> 25:19.935
You heard the same thing
over and over again,

25:20.018 --> 25:23.939
so whether you liked each other or not,
it was subconsciously ingrained in you.

25:26.233 --> 25:28.235
So I was a victim of gaslighting?

25:28.318 --> 25:30.528
Do paramedics carry air rifles?

25:30.612 --> 25:32.822
-I want to shoot him.
-What?

25:32.906 --> 25:34.824
Maybe I should've become a cop.

25:34.908 --> 25:36.034
No, you're fine as is.

25:36.117 --> 25:39.120
Hey, but the thing is

25:39.204 --> 25:42.916
all three of us hung out together,
so why did people put us two together?

25:42.999 --> 25:45.877
That's because I'm way out of his league.

25:48.713 --> 25:50.006
Yeah, it's okay.

25:50.090 --> 25:53.718
Her sights have always been
out of this world.

25:53.802 --> 25:56.221
Her standards of beauty
are different from ours.

25:56.304 --> 25:57.222
That is true.

25:59.349 --> 26:02.227
By the way, you look cool today.
Why are you in uniform?

26:02.310 --> 26:03.937
-Good question.
-Well…

26:04.020 --> 26:06.147
I had an interview today.

26:06.773 --> 26:09.276
The South Pole position?
Your application passed?

26:09.359 --> 26:11.069
Of course!

26:11.152 --> 26:12.404
Wait a second.

26:12.487 --> 26:14.447
Are you really going to go
if you pass this too?

26:14.531 --> 26:16.074
Wow!

26:16.157 --> 26:19.327
Then, does that mean
you'll get to see penguins in person?

26:19.411 --> 26:20.829
Penguins right before your eyes?

26:20.912 --> 26:21.913
That's right.

26:21.997 --> 26:23.290
-Take a lot of pictures--
-No.

26:23.373 --> 26:27.794
In Antarctica, the penguins are in danger
due to the climate crisis.

26:27.877 --> 26:29.504
Polar bears are in danger too.

26:30.672 --> 26:31.506
I'm home.

26:31.589 --> 26:33.550
-Hi.
-Mo-eum!

26:33.633 --> 26:36.594
Yeon-du!

26:36.678 --> 26:39.723
What were you up to?

26:39.806 --> 26:41.891
What were you doing, Yeon-du?

26:43.184 --> 26:45.520
What have you been doing all day?

26:46.021 --> 26:47.731
We read books together.

26:47.814 --> 26:50.358
-Okay.
-And we removed the guts from anchovies.

26:50.442 --> 26:51.693
You did?

26:53.570 --> 26:57.449
Mom, did you make Yeon-du
remove the guts from anchovies?

26:57.532 --> 27:00.327
Are you Cinderella's stepmother?

27:00.410 --> 27:02.370
Seriously?

27:02.454 --> 27:06.041
No. It looked fun,
so I said wanted to help.

27:06.833 --> 27:07.834
Really?

27:08.376 --> 27:11.880
Jeez. Did you think your own mother
would abuse a child?

27:11.963 --> 27:14.841
No. I just wanted to make sure.

27:14.924 --> 27:16.426
Yeon-du.

27:16.926 --> 27:20.013
I'll take the anchovies
we prepared together,

27:20.096 --> 27:21.973
and I'll stir-fry them nice and well!

27:22.057 --> 27:23.433
Okay, thank you!

27:23.516 --> 27:24.517
That sounds so good.

27:24.601 --> 27:26.227
It sounds so good!

27:28.688 --> 27:32.650
Hey, if you're not going to get married,

27:32.734 --> 27:36.071
go somewhere and bring back
a daughter like Yeon-du.

27:36.154 --> 27:37.155
What?

27:37.238 --> 27:40.200
That's how badly I want
a grandchild of my own. Okay?

27:40.283 --> 27:41.785
Go and stir-fry the anchovies.

27:41.868 --> 27:43.620
I swear…

27:49.000 --> 27:52.420
Yeon-du, aren't you bored
from just reading books all day?

27:53.963 --> 27:55.423
I don't know.

27:58.385 --> 28:02.263
Is there anything else you want to do
besides reading books?

28:02.347 --> 28:04.015
Want to go ride bikes?

28:04.099 --> 28:05.767
I don't know how to.

28:05.850 --> 28:06.768
Really?

28:08.186 --> 28:10.188
Then…

28:10.271 --> 28:12.982
-How about scooters?
-I can't ride those either.

28:15.110 --> 28:16.736
You don't like to play outside?

28:16.820 --> 28:21.491
It's not that, but my dad says
it's too dangerous outside.

28:22.784 --> 28:23.952
I see.

28:28.915 --> 28:30.291
It's you!

28:30.375 --> 28:33.670
Rock, paper, scissors, shoot!
Minus one!

28:33.753 --> 28:34.796
Ribbit, ribbit!

28:34.879 --> 28:37.340
Rock, paper, scissors, shoot!
Minus one!

28:37.424 --> 28:38.716
-Yeon-du.
-Ribbit!

28:39.300 --> 28:40.343
Dad!

28:43.096 --> 28:47.809
Yeon-du, I missed you so much today.

28:47.892 --> 28:49.477
Did you miss me too?

28:49.561 --> 28:50.729
Well…

28:50.812 --> 28:52.897
Yeah, I'd say so.

28:57.569 --> 29:00.780
Thank you. I owe you a lot.

29:00.864 --> 29:03.867
No, it's fine. Do you have work tomorrow?

29:03.950 --> 29:05.160
-Yes.
-I see.

29:06.244 --> 29:07.871
-Take a day off.
-Sorry?

29:07.954 --> 29:09.914
Let's meet here at 10:00 a.m. tomorrow.

29:09.998 --> 29:10.832
But…

29:10.915 --> 29:12.167
-No refusals.
-Wait.

29:12.250 --> 29:13.293
No questions.

29:13.376 --> 29:14.335
But…

29:15.003 --> 29:16.921
And no mudflat shirt.

29:18.631 --> 29:20.884
-Yeon-du, see you tomorrow.
-See you tomorrow!

29:20.967 --> 29:22.135
-Ribbit!
-Ribbit!

29:23.928 --> 29:25.388
Dad, let's go.

29:28.057 --> 29:32.020
Hey, isn't this the tree I gave to you?

29:33.313 --> 29:34.731
Did you kill it and buy a new one?

29:34.814 --> 29:35.982
That's right.

29:36.065 --> 29:36.941
How did you know?

29:37.650 --> 29:39.027
That's the secret of its origin.

29:41.821 --> 29:44.324
It's grown so much. This is so neat.

29:44.407 --> 29:45.992
How did it grow so much?

29:46.534 --> 29:47.744
-Seok-ryu.
-Yeah?

29:49.788 --> 29:50.663
Are you…

29:51.039 --> 29:52.791
Are you going to go on that blind date?

29:52.874 --> 29:56.795
Are you crazy?
I'll make something up and turn her down.

29:58.254 --> 30:00.840
This won't do.
Let's just tell her we're dating.

30:00.924 --> 30:01.758
What?

30:01.841 --> 30:03.968
Who knows? This might happen again.

30:04.761 --> 30:06.554
Let's also tell your dad.

30:06.638 --> 30:10.225
We'll tell my parents too.
Let's officially get their approval.

30:11.184 --> 30:13.144
We should tell the entire neighborhood.

30:13.228 --> 30:14.437
We can't.

30:15.897 --> 30:17.148
-Why not?
-I mean…

30:17.232 --> 30:19.234
We've just started to date.

30:19.317 --> 30:22.111
Telling everyone seems a bit too much.

30:23.404 --> 30:25.406
It's pretty obvious that it'll be chaos.

30:26.783 --> 30:30.411
It's a little bit of an issue.
Our moms are friends.

30:30.495 --> 30:32.372
And we're all so close.

30:32.455 --> 30:37.168
And to be honest, you don't know
what could happen to us.

30:40.839 --> 30:42.131
Let's keep it a secret for now.

30:44.050 --> 30:47.178
All right. If that's what you want…

30:48.972 --> 30:50.974
Let's keep our relationship a secret.

30:51.057 --> 30:52.058
Top secret.

30:52.141 --> 30:54.227
We have to be diligent. No one can know.

30:54.769 --> 30:55.770
No one will know.

31:10.201 --> 31:11.327
Is he up?

31:17.000 --> 31:20.003
Choisseung.

31:23.548 --> 31:25.216
Bonjour, Seok-ryu!

31:25.300 --> 31:26.968
-Aunt Hye-suk!
-Hi.

31:27.051 --> 31:30.096
Seung-hyo went to work early today.
Is it urgent?

31:30.179 --> 31:32.348
No, it's nothing.

31:32.432 --> 31:35.476
Hey, I didn't know your windows
were this close.

31:35.560 --> 31:37.395
You could trip and kiss each other.

31:38.521 --> 31:41.482
I bet you two hardly ever spent
any time apart.

31:41.566 --> 31:42.984
That's right.

31:43.067 --> 31:46.571
That's why I'm so sick of it!

31:46.654 --> 31:48.323
I bet Choisseung feels the same.

31:48.406 --> 31:51.117
But still, don't fight
and try to get along, okay?

31:51.200 --> 31:52.744
Okay.

31:52.827 --> 31:54.495
-I have something on the stove.
-Go ahead!

31:54.579 --> 31:56.331
Sorry. I'll see you next time. Bye!

31:59.834 --> 32:00.919
Gosh, that scared me.

32:08.092 --> 32:09.510
BAE SEOK-RYU

32:16.267 --> 32:18.436
BAE SEOK-RYU

32:24.067 --> 32:25.485
-Na-yun.
-Yes?

32:25.568 --> 32:26.903
What did you just do?

32:28.655 --> 32:29.656
Well…

32:36.996 --> 32:38.873
You know what you did
was excessive, right?

32:39.874 --> 32:40.708
Yes.

32:40.792 --> 32:43.419
I've allowed your actions to slide

32:43.503 --> 32:45.922
because I thought of you
as just a cute former classmate.

32:46.923 --> 32:48.132
But I can't anymore.

32:48.883 --> 32:50.385
I'm sorry for what I just did.

32:51.552 --> 32:53.221
But, Seung-hyo,

32:53.304 --> 32:55.223
you know that I like you.

32:55.306 --> 32:57.642
I thought it was half crush, half joking.

32:57.725 --> 33:00.812
No, it's not. I'm serious.

33:00.895 --> 33:03.231
Then, I think I need
to be perfectly clear.

33:04.399 --> 33:06.067
There's someone else I like.

33:07.485 --> 33:08.903
Is it someone I know?

33:10.613 --> 33:13.658
She's someone I found
after a long and difficult journey.

33:14.450 --> 33:17.787
I don't want to do anything
that would make her feel uncomfortable.

33:34.429 --> 33:37.432
I'm sorry I didn't pick up.
Want to see a movie later?

33:37.515 --> 33:40.601
What is this? Is he officially
asking me out on a date?

33:40.685 --> 33:41.686
Sounds good.

33:45.148 --> 33:47.150
I have to wash my hair.

33:49.652 --> 33:51.904
-Mo-eum!
-Yeon-du!

33:51.988 --> 33:55.742
My sweet Yeon-du!

33:57.535 --> 33:58.619
Did you sleep well?

33:58.703 --> 34:00.371
Any dreams about being
an alien's friend?

34:00.455 --> 34:02.373
No, I dreamt of something else.

34:02.457 --> 34:03.541
What was it?

34:03.624 --> 34:06.335
It's a secret. I'll tell you later.

34:06.419 --> 34:07.545
Okay.

34:10.006 --> 34:11.382
You're very punctual.

34:11.466 --> 34:12.925
It's the basics of being a reporter.

34:13.551 --> 34:15.511
I came because you asked me to, but…

34:15.595 --> 34:18.014
I don't need to say
where we're going, right?

34:21.476 --> 34:22.810
Let's go!

34:22.894 --> 34:24.771
Dad, bring that stuff and follow us!

34:24.854 --> 34:26.064
-What?
-What?

34:26.147 --> 34:28.066
-We're not going to help?
-The car's over there.

34:28.149 --> 34:28.983
Ms. Jung?

34:54.509 --> 34:56.052
I'll just do it.

34:56.135 --> 34:56.969
No, it's fine.

34:57.053 --> 34:58.805
-I'll do it.
-Dad.

35:00.306 --> 35:01.432
-Dad?
-Yeah?

35:24.914 --> 35:27.166
You can do it, Dad.

35:29.585 --> 35:30.628
Careful, it's hot.

35:32.338 --> 35:33.172
Try some.

35:33.256 --> 35:34.924
-I'll eat it on my own.
-Okay.

35:41.055 --> 35:43.474
-Is it good?
-You're pretty good at grilling!

35:44.934 --> 35:46.561
What are we doing next, Mo-eum?

35:46.644 --> 35:48.688
What we're going to do next is…

35:51.524 --> 35:53.484
-Wow!
-Wow!

35:57.405 --> 36:00.074
Don't shoot Yeon-du!

36:09.375 --> 36:12.044
I give up!

36:19.468 --> 36:21.846
You're drenched.

36:24.599 --> 36:26.100
I was able to borrow this.

36:27.894 --> 36:30.188
But we don't have any electricity.
How can we use that?

36:30.938 --> 36:31.814
Just a second.

36:49.582 --> 36:50.833
Wow!

36:51.459 --> 36:52.627
Wow!

36:52.710 --> 36:53.836
I'll dry your hair, Yeon-du.

36:54.295 --> 36:55.546
Let's dry your hair.

36:57.131 --> 36:58.925
What was most fun for you?

36:59.008 --> 37:00.885
I liked playing
with the water guns the most.

37:00.968 --> 37:02.178
Me too.

37:13.064 --> 37:14.357
All done.

37:16.776 --> 37:18.527
Yeon-du!

37:18.611 --> 37:21.030
I'll tie your hair nice and pretty later.

37:21.113 --> 37:23.824
-Okay.
-Your hair's wet too.

37:23.908 --> 37:25.284
I'll dry it myself.

37:25.368 --> 37:26.369
What?

37:28.579 --> 37:29.956
I see! Right!

37:51.394 --> 37:52.812
I thought you might be cold.

37:54.355 --> 37:56.732
Yeon-du, how about we go over there?

37:59.360 --> 38:00.278
Where?

38:31.350 --> 38:32.351
Hey, Choisseung.

38:32.852 --> 38:33.769
Hey.

38:36.147 --> 38:38.107
I'm here and you won't even look at me?

38:39.442 --> 38:40.443
I did look.

38:45.448 --> 38:47.241
What are you so busy with?

38:47.325 --> 38:50.661
I was tasked with remodeling
a movie theater.

38:50.745 --> 38:52.705
I thought of something when I got here,

38:52.788 --> 38:54.373
so I wanted to draw it before I forgot.

38:56.250 --> 38:57.168
Will it take long?

38:57.251 --> 38:59.545
No, I'll be done
before the movie starts.

39:05.092 --> 39:07.053
So this is what a blueprint looks like.

39:08.763 --> 39:09.638
Yeah.

39:14.268 --> 39:16.228
Do you want popcorn? I'll buy some.

39:16.896 --> 39:18.064
No, I'm fine.

39:18.147 --> 39:22.651
Really? Then, I'll just buy a drink.

39:23.319 --> 39:24.153
Okay.

39:51.639 --> 39:52.807
What? Do you want more?

39:59.647 --> 40:00.731
Sorry.

40:02.483 --> 40:03.317
What do we do?

40:03.401 --> 40:06.404
They said they'd analyze the photos
and bring them here in 30 minutes.

40:06.487 --> 40:07.988
-Mi-ja.
-Okay, stop there.

40:08.072 --> 40:09.573
Just a moment. One second.

40:17.581 --> 40:19.500
The sun is already setting.

40:21.627 --> 40:23.546
Should we go before it gets too late?

40:24.171 --> 40:25.005
No.

40:26.006 --> 40:29.510
Yeon-du just fell asleep.
Let's stay for 30 more minutes.

40:29.593 --> 40:30.594
Okay.

40:37.768 --> 40:39.728
She must be heavy. Give her to me.

40:42.356 --> 40:44.400
Yeon-du, let's sleep on the bed.

40:47.111 --> 40:48.070
It was fine though.

40:58.998 --> 41:00.291
So how was camping?

41:02.084 --> 41:03.085
Not bad, right?

41:03.794 --> 41:04.628
Yeah.

41:06.046 --> 41:07.506
I've never thought about it,

41:08.924 --> 41:10.468
but Yeon-du really liked it.

41:11.802 --> 41:14.722
Yeon-du said she couldn't ride a bike.

41:16.182 --> 41:19.018
She can't ride scooters
or rollerblade either.

41:22.521 --> 41:25.566
It's because of the accident, right?

41:28.444 --> 41:30.196
It wasn't on purpose.

41:31.947 --> 41:36.494
I just keep getting so worried.

41:37.244 --> 41:38.579
I understand how you feel.

41:39.997 --> 41:44.043
I know I have no authority
to tell you what to do either.

41:44.752 --> 41:46.045
But…

41:48.088 --> 41:51.050
if you keep a miracle
hidden away like that,

41:51.884 --> 41:53.928
it'll never really be a miracle.

41:56.555 --> 42:02.311
I want Yeon-du to feel the wind
and stomp her feet.

42:03.103 --> 42:07.733
And sometimes, she'll fall down.

42:09.610 --> 42:12.446
That's how I'd want her to grow.

42:14.949 --> 42:19.495
I want her to see and hear
all the good things in this world.

42:19.578 --> 42:25.417
I hope she can take it all in
like a sponge and grow healthy.

42:30.089 --> 42:31.799
Wouldn't that be a real miracle?

42:34.635 --> 42:36.095
I'm so sorry to Yeon-du.

42:38.264 --> 42:41.350
It would've been nice
if I was as brave as you.

42:50.985 --> 42:54.321
Sometimes, I think it would be nice
if I was Yeon-du's mom.

43:01.120 --> 43:03.914
Come on. Still, that's a bit much.

43:04.582 --> 43:05.499
I can't?

43:09.086 --> 43:11.630
I know I'm moving really fast right now.

43:12.339 --> 43:15.801
It's like I've just traveled to Andromeda
over 2.5 million light-years away.

43:15.884 --> 43:16.885
But…

43:18.596 --> 43:20.014
that's how I feel right now.

43:21.682 --> 43:23.225
Ms. Jung…

43:24.059 --> 43:26.103
My heart races whenever I see you.

43:27.855 --> 43:31.191
It beats rapidly like a drum every time.

43:32.443 --> 43:36.614
I even see you in my dreams too.

43:40.743 --> 43:41.785
So I was wondering.

43:42.786 --> 43:43.996
About our kiss…

43:45.581 --> 43:47.750
Can't we cancel our agreement?

43:49.335 --> 43:50.919
I don't think it was a mistake.

44:01.263 --> 44:04.183
No, we can't. Never.

44:06.060 --> 44:08.187
Yeon-du can't become your daughter.

44:08.270 --> 44:10.022
And what happened that day was a mistake.

44:11.357 --> 44:12.274
It has to be.

44:14.234 --> 44:15.194
Why?

44:18.572 --> 44:19.865
Because it can't happen.

44:30.167 --> 44:32.586
From now on,
I won't leave Yeon-du at your house.

44:33.545 --> 44:36.840
And I'd appreciate it
if you didn't hang out with her anymore.

44:36.924 --> 44:38.801
-Dan-ho…
-We should go.

44:40.928 --> 44:41.929
Yeon-du.

44:42.554 --> 44:44.973
Wake up. We have to go home.

44:46.642 --> 44:49.144
Let's sleep in the car, okay?

45:20.259 --> 45:21.552
Go on in first.

45:21.635 --> 45:22.553
What? Why?

45:22.636 --> 45:25.222
What if we run into
your mom again like last time?

45:25.305 --> 45:28.058
Come on. We've hung around
with each other for years.

45:28.142 --> 45:30.144
-She won't be suspicious of this.
-But still…

45:30.227 --> 45:33.147
To keep this secret, we need to be careful
around the neighborhood.

45:33.230 --> 45:35.858
I'll take a lap around the block.
Go on in first.

45:36.567 --> 45:37.484
Okay, then.

45:46.452 --> 45:48.829
Since when did he start
listening to me so well?

45:50.080 --> 45:51.039
Ridiculous.

46:02.593 --> 46:04.178
Alzheimer's…

46:07.556 --> 46:08.974
-It's not that.
-Really?

46:09.057 --> 46:10.392
-Yes.
-Really?

46:10.476 --> 46:12.603
Take a look for yourself
if you don't believe me.

46:12.686 --> 46:15.647
Hey, you're going to break it!

46:15.731 --> 46:17.608
There's nothing wrong with her brain.

46:17.691 --> 46:18.859
Of course,

46:18.942 --> 46:21.778
we'll have to see if your symptoms
reoccur in the future.

46:21.862 --> 46:24.740
Then, why did I keep forgetting things?

46:24.823 --> 46:27.493
You could say
it's a type of short-term memory loss.

46:27.576 --> 46:29.036
I see.

46:29.119 --> 46:33.373
Have you experienced any shock
or a significant amount of stress lately?

46:37.836 --> 46:39.129
Yes.

46:39.213 --> 46:41.840
Then, it could be from that stress.

46:41.924 --> 46:44.176
It could be due to heightened anxiety.

46:44.259 --> 46:47.137
If you rest and take care of yourself,
you'll be fine.

46:48.138 --> 46:49.139
Thank you.

46:56.855 --> 46:58.482
I'm so relieved.

46:58.565 --> 47:01.693
No, "relieved" isn't enough
to describe how I feel.

47:01.777 --> 47:05.822
I've been in an emotional hell
for the past two weeks.

47:05.906 --> 47:08.200
You said it would be okay,

47:08.283 --> 47:11.203
but I thought of the worst-case scenarios.

47:12.621 --> 47:14.081
Are you listening to me?

47:15.499 --> 47:16.416
Honey!

47:17.584 --> 47:18.585
Honey, what's wrong?

47:22.256 --> 47:24.132
Honey, what's the matter? What is it?

47:24.800 --> 47:27.261
What? Honey, don't cry. What's wrong?

47:27.844 --> 47:30.847
I thought something bad
was going to happen to you.

47:32.724 --> 47:35.477
I just learned the truth not too long ago,

47:36.687 --> 47:40.023
and I was finally able to express
my true feelings.

47:42.276 --> 47:44.444
But I was afraid I was too late.

47:47.322 --> 47:49.700
I was afraid you'd forget me.

47:52.578 --> 47:54.830
I was scared I'd lose you.

47:56.081 --> 47:58.041
Honey.

47:58.125 --> 48:01.003
I can't live without you, Hye-suk!

48:05.424 --> 48:06.925
For goodness' sake.

48:09.678 --> 48:11.471
I swear.

48:11.555 --> 48:14.474
You've been embarrassing me
a lot these days, you know.

48:16.852 --> 48:18.687
But this isn't so bad either.

48:20.939 --> 48:22.190
Honey.

48:24.693 --> 48:26.945
He said I didn't have Alzheimer's!

48:28.614 --> 48:30.741
Stop crying, Gyeong-jong!

48:30.824 --> 48:33.035
Why didn't you say
anything like this before?

48:33.118 --> 48:35.370
You big dummy!

49:09.112 --> 49:10.364
See you next class!

49:10.447 --> 49:11.740
-Bye!
-Bye!

49:17.579 --> 49:19.164
-Hello?
-Hey, Choisseung.

49:19.247 --> 49:22.918
So I made neobiani in class today.

49:23.001 --> 49:24.795
It's so good. Want me to bring you some?

49:24.878 --> 49:26.963
I had work to do outside,
so I'm not at the office.

49:27.047 --> 49:29.049
Do you want to come by later at night?

49:29.132 --> 49:31.593
-At night?
-Yeah.

49:31.677 --> 49:32.969
Seung-hyo!

49:34.179 --> 49:36.306
I have to go. I'll see you later.

49:41.853 --> 49:42.771
At night?

49:44.272 --> 49:45.899
If it's at night…

49:46.608 --> 49:51.988
Then, it'll be dark
and no one will be around.

49:59.037 --> 50:00.664
ORDER DETAILS

50:00.747 --> 50:04.084
What? I made the post days ago,
but why are there only ten orders?

50:07.754 --> 50:09.047
Damn it.

50:15.137 --> 50:16.722
Were my abs not defined enough?

50:19.224 --> 50:20.934
I should've worked out a bit more.

50:22.394 --> 50:23.562
JAE-YEONG

50:24.479 --> 50:25.814
Hey, Jae-yeong.

50:26.815 --> 50:27.899
What? Haeundae Beach?

50:28.608 --> 50:30.485
I'm in no position to go now…

50:31.862 --> 50:33.905
Really? I don't have to pay?

50:35.824 --> 50:37.284
You're paying?

50:37.367 --> 50:38.702
Choisseung!

50:39.536 --> 50:41.580
I made a lot of good food…

50:43.498 --> 50:44.541
for us.

50:47.502 --> 50:49.629
You're all here.

50:50.714 --> 50:51.965
It's been a while, Seok-ryu.

50:52.048 --> 50:53.049
Hi.

51:00.098 --> 51:04.019
My goodness! This was made with such care!

51:04.102 --> 51:05.979
Why did you bring so much food?

51:07.147 --> 51:10.233
You must've come
to congratulate Seung-hyo.

51:10.317 --> 51:11.234
Congratulate him?

51:11.318 --> 51:14.279
Yes. To celebrate the launch
of the collaboration with Fresco,

51:14.362 --> 51:15.363
they interviewed him.

51:15.447 --> 51:17.157
Hey, that article should be out now.

51:17.240 --> 51:18.450
-Show it to her.
-Right.

51:19.659 --> 51:21.161
I've been looking at it for a while.

51:22.662 --> 51:24.206
The picture came out well too.

51:24.915 --> 51:28.210
I was going to leave right after,
but Myeong-u told me to stay.

51:28.293 --> 51:30.879
Aren't you glad I did?
You get to try all this good food.

51:30.962 --> 51:32.297
Whatever.

51:32.380 --> 51:34.341
I've finished my coffee, so I'll go.

51:34.424 --> 51:35.926
What? You're leaving and not eating?

51:36.009 --> 51:37.219
I'm busy.

51:38.428 --> 51:40.639
-You're going to go?
-Yes.

51:40.722 --> 51:43.600
I did want to congratulate you,

51:43.683 --> 51:45.352
so I'm glad I can.

51:46.937 --> 51:50.607
Congratulations
on your official start to cooking.

51:51.107 --> 51:53.944
It was thanks to your advice. Thank you.

51:54.027 --> 51:56.154
It was thanks to your delicious kalguksu.

51:58.573 --> 52:00.242
Great job today. I'm off.

52:00.325 --> 52:02.244
All right, get home safe.

52:02.327 --> 52:04.412
-Thanks.
-Good night.

52:04.496 --> 52:06.289
Bye. Thanks. Great job.

52:06.373 --> 52:07.958
-Get home safe.
-Thanks.

52:11.753 --> 52:13.797
It would've been nice if she stayed.

52:35.944 --> 52:39.781
I texted you and said I'd call you later
since tonight wasn't a good night.

52:44.244 --> 52:45.453
I saw it just now.

52:48.290 --> 52:50.500
Why didn't you tell me
you had an interview with Fresco?

52:51.459 --> 52:52.794
Was it because of Tae-hui?

52:52.878 --> 52:56.131
They said it wouldn't take long,
so I was going to tell you after.

52:56.214 --> 52:58.133
-But it ended up like this.
-What?

52:58.216 --> 53:00.093
You thought I wouldn't understand?

53:00.176 --> 53:02.053
No, it's not that.

53:05.974 --> 53:07.684
I'm sorry. I have no excuse.

53:09.144 --> 53:11.396
It was nice seeing her
after all this time.

53:12.147 --> 53:13.148
She's still pretty.

53:13.231 --> 53:15.609
Tae-hui didn't come
because she wanted to either.

53:15.692 --> 53:17.694
Myeong-u kept insisting.

53:17.777 --> 53:20.113
Did you tell her we're dating?

53:20.196 --> 53:21.031
No.

53:23.825 --> 53:25.493
You told me not to tell anyone.

53:25.577 --> 53:26.703
But an ex-girlfriend

53:27.370 --> 53:28.413
is different…

53:33.418 --> 53:34.419
Okay.

53:35.128 --> 53:38.089
Also, we didn't have time
to talk about anything personal.

53:38.173 --> 53:40.050
It was an official event.

53:41.551 --> 53:44.554
Now that I think about it,
you two are like Hollywood actors.

53:45.388 --> 53:48.934
I could never work with my ex-boyfriend.

53:50.226 --> 53:51.186
I mean, think about it.

53:51.269 --> 53:53.855
Even if you try,
feelings don't just disappear.

53:53.939 --> 53:54.981
And things were once good.

53:55.649 --> 53:57.025
It's all in the past.

53:58.109 --> 53:59.736
I want to stop talking about this.

53:59.819 --> 54:02.989
What's wrong? I know everything anyway.

54:03.573 --> 54:07.327
Hey, when you told
Tae-hui earlier to get home safe,

54:07.410 --> 54:08.662
your voice was no joke.

54:08.745 --> 54:10.497
-It was so deep.
-I never did that.

54:10.580 --> 54:13.541
You did. You were so worried about her.

54:13.625 --> 54:16.169
I mean, why didn't you just take her home?

54:16.252 --> 54:17.087
Seok-ryu.

54:17.170 --> 54:19.297
How were you around her
when I wasn't here?

54:19.381 --> 54:22.842
Were you mature
and understanding around her?

54:27.514 --> 54:29.015
I don't want to answer that.

54:33.311 --> 54:36.022
I'm not obligated
to tell you things like that.

55:05.093 --> 55:06.803
What's wrong with me?

55:16.813 --> 55:18.690
You have some nerve, Choi Seung-hyo.

55:27.532 --> 55:28.783
Are you heading out now?

55:28.867 --> 55:30.410
Yes. Where are you going?

55:30.493 --> 55:32.120
I'm going to Seoraksan Mountain.

55:32.203 --> 55:35.123
Your father and I are taking
an overnight trip with Seok-ryu's parents.

55:35.790 --> 55:38.043
I forgot to tell you.

55:39.377 --> 55:42.172
You're staying one night.
Why did you pack so much?

55:42.255 --> 55:46.551
No. The thing is, your dad…

55:46.634 --> 55:48.678
What is all this?

55:48.762 --> 55:50.430
Compression bandages and heat packs.

55:50.513 --> 55:52.974
Your ankle hasn't fully healed yet,
so it's just in case.

55:53.058 --> 55:55.643
I have acupressure patches
if your feet hurt from walking a lot.

55:55.727 --> 55:58.021
Why not bring crutches
and a wheelchair too?

55:58.104 --> 55:59.189
You think I should?

55:59.272 --> 56:00.315
I'll call the hospital.

56:00.398 --> 56:02.108
No, honey. It's fine.

56:02.192 --> 56:04.736
Come here! We're late. Let's go. Jeez!

56:06.154 --> 56:08.073
So that's what Dad's really like.

56:10.283 --> 56:11.868
I said hurry up!

56:11.951 --> 56:14.329
Honey, you washed my pants wrong.
They shrank!

56:14.412 --> 56:16.956
-You should've washed them right.
-Honey, they're mine.

56:18.249 --> 56:20.126
-They're not mine?
-Seriously?

56:20.210 --> 56:21.544
I see. It has a lace trim.

56:21.628 --> 56:23.421
I told you to pack earlier!

56:23.505 --> 56:26.216
I don't have any tank tops!
Is there a black hole in the drawer?

56:26.299 --> 56:27.967
I can't find anything in this house.

56:28.051 --> 56:30.220
Seok-ryu, your dad
would be a perfect slug.

56:30.303 --> 56:32.305
-A slug!
-Is that how you talk of your husband?

56:32.388 --> 56:33.765
You turn me into a slug?

56:33.848 --> 56:34.933
When are you leaving?

56:35.016 --> 56:37.352
-It's been 30 minutes!
-Why are you looking for that now?

56:37.435 --> 56:39.270
We'll probably go tomorrow
thanks to your dad!

56:39.354 --> 56:41.189
My tank top. My sunglasses are gone!

56:41.272 --> 56:44.192
-Find my sunglasses.
-Dad, they're on your head!

56:44.692 --> 56:45.777
There they are!

56:45.860 --> 56:47.987
Jeez! And where are you going?

56:48.071 --> 56:49.864
What? I'm going to Busan with my friends.

56:49.948 --> 56:52.784
-Wow, you're all going without me?
-Here it is. Here!

56:52.867 --> 56:55.036
Jeez, it was right there!
How could you not find it?

56:55.120 --> 56:56.371
-I caught it.
-Good grief.

56:56.454 --> 56:58.331
-Let's take these!
-Where's Dong-jin going?

56:58.414 --> 57:00.416
-Busan with his friends.
-All of a sudden?

57:00.500 --> 57:02.001
Dad, could you not wear those?

57:02.085 --> 57:03.545
-No, I need these.
-Goodness.

57:03.628 --> 57:06.256
-Don't wear those at Seoraksan.
-That's a fashion crime.

57:07.465 --> 57:09.884
Sorry! He kept on dawdling.

57:09.968 --> 57:11.219
It's okay. We didn't wait much.

57:11.302 --> 57:14.097
Gosh, you took forever
in front of the mirror picking scarves!

57:14.180 --> 57:15.473
-"This or that?"
-Let's go!

57:15.557 --> 57:16.474
-Okay!
-Okay!

57:17.433 --> 57:18.434
-Get in.
-Here.

57:18.518 --> 57:19.602
Thanks, honey.

57:21.729 --> 57:23.273
-Here.
-Honey, get in.

57:23.356 --> 57:24.315
Honey?

57:24.816 --> 57:29.028
The car looks so sleek and shiny.
I've always wanted to go for a ride in it.

57:30.321 --> 57:32.282
Wow!

57:32.365 --> 57:33.950
Is this your first time in our car?

57:34.033 --> 57:35.869
-Yes.
-I see.

57:37.036 --> 57:39.080
GANGNEUNG DAEGWALLYEONG SERVICE AREA

57:39.164 --> 57:40.165
Are we almost there?

57:40.248 --> 57:41.291
-Yeah.
-Honey!

57:41.374 --> 57:43.543
-The water's so cold.
-Here. Dry your hands.

57:43.960 --> 57:46.004
Thanks. The water was so cold.

57:46.087 --> 57:47.464
-Really? No hot water?
-No.

57:47.547 --> 57:48.548
That's terrible.

57:51.509 --> 57:55.889
Honey! Man, these have
entire walnuts in them!

57:55.972 --> 57:57.056
My hands feel frozen.

57:57.140 --> 57:59.476
-That's cold. Hey!
-Hey!

57:59.559 --> 58:01.144
-You're so rude.
-Come on.

58:01.227 --> 58:03.396
I think it got on my face. Look.

58:03.480 --> 58:04.898
-Geun-sik!
-Goodness.

58:04.981 --> 58:07.442
-Just lightly pat it.
-Do you have a handkerchief?

58:07.525 --> 58:08.735
A handkerchief?

58:08.818 --> 58:11.529
Yeah. But I used this
to blow my nose. Is that okay?

58:11.613 --> 58:13.490
You're so rude.

58:13.573 --> 58:15.366
-What's wrong?
-I want those walnut pastries.

58:15.450 --> 58:17.118
Do you want some of these?

58:17.202 --> 58:19.913
Wow! Let's take a picture here!

58:19.996 --> 58:22.540
Mi-suk, let's take
our individual pictures first.

58:22.624 --> 58:23.583
-Individual ones?
-Yeah.

58:23.666 --> 58:25.043
Take a picture of me.

58:25.126 --> 58:26.211
-Just a second.
-Okay.

58:26.294 --> 58:27.962
Honey, take a picture of me with this.

58:28.046 --> 58:29.756
-Just take it yourself.
-No, with the bear!

58:29.839 --> 58:31.216
For goodness' sake.

58:31.674 --> 58:32.759
-With the bear?
-Yeah.

58:32.842 --> 58:34.302
-Okay.
-But…

58:34.385 --> 58:35.970
That's how you get the bear in it.

58:36.054 --> 58:37.680
No, take some more.

58:37.764 --> 58:39.349
-Jeez.
-This weather is amazing.

58:39.432 --> 58:40.391
It's unbelievable.

58:42.352 --> 58:43.603
Goodness.

58:46.397 --> 58:47.982
Should I stand here? How do I look?

58:48.066 --> 58:49.651
That's good, honey.

58:49.734 --> 58:51.444
Who carries around something like that?

58:51.528 --> 58:54.113
-It is heavy.
-Goodness. What is he doing?

58:54.197 --> 58:55.657
Now, that's funny.

58:56.324 --> 58:57.325
Goodness.

58:57.408 --> 58:58.535
He's going crazy now.

58:58.618 --> 59:01.371
You two have both gone crazy.

59:01.454 --> 59:03.373
-Is that okay?
-Let's see that jawline!

59:03.456 --> 59:04.832
-I feel embarrassed.
-Goodness.

59:04.916 --> 59:06.000
-Nice!
-What's with you?

59:06.084 --> 59:07.544
-Good!
-What are you doing?

59:07.627 --> 59:09.546
-Great!
-Let me see.

59:09.629 --> 59:11.881
-I'm next!
-No, let's look.

59:13.007 --> 59:14.217
Honey.

59:14.717 --> 59:16.886
Since when did you take
such great pictures?

59:16.970 --> 59:20.723
I went online and studied how to take
good pictures of your girlfriend.

59:22.517 --> 59:23.851
Do you like it?

59:23.935 --> 59:26.020
I love it. You did great. It's amazing.

59:26.104 --> 59:29.524
You idiot. You made me look like a dwarf.

59:29.607 --> 59:31.442
It looks just like you.

59:31.526 --> 59:33.236
Hey, Gyeong-jong.

59:33.319 --> 59:35.029
Can you take a picture
of me with that too?

59:35.572 --> 59:37.156
-Yeah, okay!
-Make my legs look long.

59:37.240 --> 59:38.449
Take your own.

59:39.659 --> 59:41.202
-Mo-eum.
-Yeah?

59:41.286 --> 59:42.829
Can you call my phone?

59:43.871 --> 59:44.747
Okay.

59:51.170 --> 59:52.714
It works.

59:53.840 --> 59:55.091
It works very well.

59:56.259 --> 59:58.553
It was so quiet I thought it was broken.

01:00:00.471 --> 01:00:03.224
SEOK-RYU

01:00:12.025 --> 01:00:12.859
Come in.

01:00:17.196 --> 01:00:18.197
-Dan-ho.
-Mr. Choi.

01:00:18.698 --> 01:00:20.950
-I mean, Mr. Kang.
-Seung-hyo.

01:00:24.370 --> 01:00:26.164
Didn't we go back to being formal?

01:00:26.247 --> 01:00:28.499
Right, we did.

01:00:29.917 --> 01:00:31.002
Take a seat.

01:00:31.085 --> 01:00:32.253
-Thank you.
-Of course.

01:00:43.139 --> 01:00:45.099
-You can sit anywhere.
-Right.

01:00:49.520 --> 01:00:52.065
I'm sorry for interrupting if you're busy.

01:00:52.148 --> 01:00:55.568
Mr. Yoon said you were in your office
and it was okay to go in.

01:00:55.652 --> 01:00:57.987
No, it's okay. I'm glad you came.

01:00:58.905 --> 01:01:00.281
But what brings you here?

01:01:00.907 --> 01:01:02.575
I have a favor to ask of you.

01:01:02.659 --> 01:01:05.453
I've been writing articles
about my experiences lately.

01:01:06.120 --> 01:01:10.416
For my next feature, I want to highlight
the lives of construction workers.

01:01:10.500 --> 01:01:14.045
I was wondering if you could
introduce me to a construction site.

01:01:16.130 --> 01:01:17.590
Of course, I can.

01:01:17.674 --> 01:01:21.344
We have a few sites under construction.
I'll call them and let you know.

01:01:21.427 --> 01:01:22.762
Thank you.

01:01:23.638 --> 01:01:25.306
I owe you a lot.

01:01:25.390 --> 01:01:29.852
Gosh, there's no need to say that.
You've helped me out a lot.

01:01:29.936 --> 01:01:31.938
You helped me catch those scammers too.

01:01:32.522 --> 01:01:34.816
-And you provided advice last time.
-I see.

01:01:37.026 --> 01:01:39.070
About your friend…

01:01:39.153 --> 01:01:42.532
May I ask how things turned out
with your friend's friend?

01:01:44.075 --> 01:01:45.785
They just recently started dating.

01:01:46.994 --> 01:01:47.829
Congratulations.

01:01:49.455 --> 01:01:51.582
I mean, congratulate your friend for me.

01:01:52.709 --> 01:01:55.628
Congratulate. Right.

01:01:56.629 --> 01:01:57.463
What's wrong?

01:01:58.339 --> 01:02:00.174
Is something not working out?

01:02:00.258 --> 01:02:02.093
No, it's just…

01:02:03.845 --> 01:02:05.471
He says dating is hard.

01:02:07.265 --> 01:02:10.727
Love is quite hard.

01:02:17.191 --> 01:02:20.445
How could he take
Tae-hui's side in front of me?

01:02:20.528 --> 01:02:22.321
I don't think he took her side.

01:02:22.405 --> 01:02:23.573
Whose side are you on?

01:02:23.656 --> 01:02:25.533
Seung-hyo, that bastard!

01:02:26.909 --> 01:02:30.538
Also, I asked him how he was
when he dated her,

01:02:31.497 --> 01:02:33.249
and he didn't want to answer.

01:02:33.332 --> 01:02:35.376
He said he wasn't obligated to tell me.

01:02:36.294 --> 01:02:39.589
Then, what answer did you want to hear?

01:02:40.923 --> 01:02:42.842
-What do you mean?
-Think about it.

01:02:42.925 --> 01:02:46.512
You'd be upset if he said
things were great with her.

01:02:46.596 --> 01:02:48.890
If he said things were awful…

01:02:48.973 --> 01:02:53.269
Would you want him to be a scumbag
who bad-mouths his ex-girlfriends?

01:02:54.854 --> 01:02:55.980
No.

01:02:56.063 --> 01:02:58.983
Right? So why would you
ask about his past?

01:02:59.484 --> 01:03:00.610
That's self-harm.

01:03:00.693 --> 01:03:02.278
You're right.

01:03:03.696 --> 01:03:05.156
I know that too.

01:03:05.239 --> 01:03:06.157
You know but what?

01:03:07.200 --> 01:03:08.576
But it makes me jealous!

01:03:13.289 --> 01:03:16.167
Hey, from now on,
I'm going to be Seung-hyo's friend.

01:03:16.250 --> 01:03:18.044
Seok-ryu, you brat!

01:03:18.127 --> 01:03:22.381
He was kind enough to let you say goodbye
to Hyeon-jun, so you can't do this to him.

01:03:22.465 --> 01:03:24.842
I know. I know that too.

01:03:25.635 --> 01:03:28.429
But I can't control how I feel,
so what can I do?

01:03:39.857 --> 01:03:43.027
She's right. You can't control feelings.

01:03:45.696 --> 01:03:46.823
Hello.

01:03:56.290 --> 01:03:57.583
There was only one left.

01:03:58.167 --> 01:03:59.001
Take this.

01:03:59.085 --> 01:04:01.254
No, it's fine. You can have it.

01:04:01.337 --> 01:04:05.383
Really, it's okay. You take it.

01:04:06.092 --> 01:04:09.595
No, I want you to have it.
It's my feelings for you.

01:04:10.805 --> 01:04:11.973
What?

01:04:14.225 --> 01:04:15.768
The fire in my heart

01:04:17.270 --> 01:04:20.940
won't be extinguished
until it's completely burned out.

01:04:23.150 --> 01:04:26.028
So, enjoy.

01:04:37.623 --> 01:04:39.709
I think I have to stop drinking this.

01:04:43.379 --> 01:04:44.797
But I don't know if I can.

01:04:50.887 --> 01:04:51.888
Stop laughing.

01:04:51.971 --> 01:04:53.514
-Do you enjoy teasing me?
-Hey.

01:04:53.598 --> 01:04:57.476
If those were signs of dementia,
we'd all be in a nursing home right now.

01:04:57.560 --> 01:05:00.396
It was really serious. I mean it.

01:05:00.479 --> 01:05:02.773
I told you. I couldn't remember anything.

01:05:02.857 --> 01:05:07.278
Hye-suk, I forgot what we had for lunch.

01:05:07.361 --> 01:05:08.195
What did we eat?

01:05:08.279 --> 01:05:10.781
Sweet and spicy chicken.
We had chicken, remember?

01:05:10.865 --> 01:05:12.199
-Sweet and spicy chicken.
-Right!

01:05:12.283 --> 01:05:13.618
-Chicken!
-Get a grip, Mi-suk.

01:05:13.701 --> 01:05:15.328
It was so crunchy and delicious!

01:05:15.411 --> 01:05:18.080
Hey, this is how we are now.

01:05:18.164 --> 01:05:20.416
Anyway, I'm so relieved that you're okay.

01:05:21.083 --> 01:05:25.463
Yeah. I learned so much
after going through this incident.

01:05:26.589 --> 01:05:28.090
Family, friends.

01:05:28.674 --> 01:05:31.010
Knowing I have people
I can lean on in my life

01:05:32.178 --> 01:05:34.221
was so reassuring.

01:05:36.223 --> 01:05:37.475
I thought that too

01:05:38.517 --> 01:05:40.561
after learning
about what happened to Seok-ryu.

01:05:42.021 --> 01:05:44.732
I wanted her to meet someone who's willing

01:05:45.650 --> 01:05:47.026
to embrace all of her pain.

01:05:47.777 --> 01:05:49.904
Someone reassuring and generous.

01:05:51.697 --> 01:05:54.075
I want to find
a nice partner for Seung-hyo too.

01:05:55.618 --> 01:05:57.870
He was lonely
for a long time because of me.

01:05:57.954 --> 01:06:02.083
Hey, let's introduce them
to good people if we find any.

01:06:02.833 --> 01:06:04.168
Let's do that.

01:06:04.251 --> 01:06:05.252
-For real!
-For real!

01:06:05.336 --> 01:06:07.421
-For real, okay?
-Yeah, for real!

01:06:07.505 --> 01:06:09.757
-Find good ones at the foreign ministry!
-For real.

01:06:09.840 --> 01:06:10.675
Okay.

01:06:10.758 --> 01:06:14.261
Hey, they left to buy alcohol,
but why aren't they back?

01:06:14.345 --> 01:06:16.681
Good question.
Are they brewing it themselves?

01:06:16.764 --> 01:06:18.849
-Did they go to karaoke?
-Those lunatics.

01:06:18.933 --> 01:06:22.478
They must be crazy.
Geun-sik mentioned his favorite song.

01:06:22.561 --> 01:06:24.188
He was talking about it earlier.

01:06:24.271 --> 01:06:26.357
-Where is it?
-That fool.

01:06:26.440 --> 01:06:27.775
-The basement!
-Basement?

01:06:27.858 --> 01:06:28.734
Let's hurry!

01:06:31.821 --> 01:06:32.655
What's that?

01:06:32.738 --> 01:06:34.657
Tae-hui kept her word.

01:06:35.324 --> 01:06:36.450
Time for the unboxing!

01:06:37.910 --> 01:06:40.246
Right. You sold me for a bowl.

01:06:41.288 --> 01:06:45.751
Seung-hyo, I might be a traitor to you,
but this was worth it. Look.

01:06:45.835 --> 01:06:46.961
Ta-da!

01:06:49.964 --> 01:06:52.633
Wow, it's beautiful.

01:06:53.384 --> 01:06:54.927
-Benedict Yoon?
-Yes?

01:06:55.011 --> 01:06:57.471
-You like it that much?
-Yes, of course.

01:06:57.555 --> 01:06:59.682
I'm going to hand this down
as a family heirloom.

01:06:59.765 --> 01:07:02.351
My future descendant will be
on Authentic Masterpieces with this,

01:07:02.435 --> 01:07:04.520
and it'll be valued at 100 billion won!

01:07:05.021 --> 01:07:07.106
I should take a picture and show my wife.

01:07:08.524 --> 01:07:09.358
Take this too.

01:07:09.442 --> 01:07:10.609
That's yours.

01:07:11.485 --> 01:07:13.195
Gosh. Mine's bigger.

01:07:26.709 --> 01:07:28.419
In a traditional wedding ceremony,

01:07:28.502 --> 01:07:31.964
the bride and groom use
a hollowed gourd split in two

01:07:32.048 --> 01:07:33.674
to share ceremonial wine.

01:07:34.925 --> 01:07:38.596
They say it symbolizes how one
is the perfect match for the other.

01:07:39.305 --> 01:07:42.433
It's my gift to you and Seok-ryu.

01:07:42.516 --> 01:07:44.935
I wish you both happiness.

01:07:49.899 --> 01:07:51.025
PRINCESS

01:07:59.617 --> 01:08:00.618
Boring.

01:08:17.426 --> 01:08:18.344
Hey.

01:08:20.638 --> 01:08:21.597
What are you doing?

01:08:22.389 --> 01:08:24.266
You have eyes. What do you think?

01:08:24.350 --> 01:08:26.644
Were you always this kind?

01:08:29.355 --> 01:08:31.857
Did you think
your boyfriend was cold-hearted?

01:08:32.983 --> 01:08:36.237
Boyfriend, my foot. Are you crazy?

01:08:38.155 --> 01:08:39.365
Wait.

01:08:40.116 --> 01:08:42.701
If I'm not your boyfriend, then what am I?

01:08:43.953 --> 01:08:46.956
I mean, you are. But…

01:08:47.748 --> 01:08:48.624
I don't know.

01:08:49.667 --> 01:08:51.669
It's just awkward to say that word.

01:08:57.341 --> 01:08:59.051
Did you make that house too?

01:09:00.136 --> 01:09:01.137
Yeah.

01:09:08.352 --> 01:09:11.522
No, stay away.
He's hurt, so he's still sensitive.

01:09:12.106 --> 01:09:14.233
I think you're the one who's sensitive.

01:09:17.736 --> 01:09:20.406
Why did you bring in a cat
if you're allergic to them?

01:09:20.489 --> 01:09:22.700
It was hurt. I couldn't just abandon it.

01:09:23.284 --> 01:09:25.452
You said you were
out of money for the snack bar.

01:09:25.536 --> 01:09:26.829
Was it for the medical expenses?

01:09:26.912 --> 01:09:30.332
Yeah, my hands are shaking
from chocolate withdrawal.

01:09:31.625 --> 01:09:32.835
But what do I do?

01:09:33.919 --> 01:09:36.172
It has nowhere to go after it heals.

01:09:37.047 --> 01:09:39.133
The weather's getting hot. Don't touch.

01:09:42.219 --> 01:09:43.387
I'm so worried.

01:10:07.578 --> 01:10:09.705
Hey, you sure you're doing it right?

01:10:09.788 --> 01:10:12.958
The roof has to be sturdy
to keep the rain and snow out.

01:10:14.335 --> 01:10:15.294
Do you want to make it?

01:10:25.054 --> 01:10:27.514
Hey, the walls have to be sturdy too.

01:10:27.598 --> 01:10:29.642
Winter will come right after summer.

01:10:32.102 --> 01:10:33.562
You'll get diabetes that way.

01:10:35.231 --> 01:10:36.440
I'll worry about myself.

01:10:43.822 --> 01:10:45.282
Wow!

01:10:45.866 --> 01:10:47.701
-Great job!
-Hey!

01:10:50.746 --> 01:10:52.456
Hey! Why you…

01:10:52.539 --> 01:10:53.582
Come on!

01:10:54.792 --> 01:10:57.002
I'm sorry! Sorry!

01:10:57.836 --> 01:10:59.463
MADE BY CHOI SEUNG-HYO

01:11:02.049 --> 01:11:03.842
I'm continuing to reconstruct it.

01:11:06.512 --> 01:11:10.516
I think the cats that use this
are descendants of the one we knew.

01:11:11.308 --> 01:11:13.394
-They have the same coat pattern.
-Really?

01:11:13.477 --> 01:11:15.813
-Yeah.
-I want to see.

01:11:15.896 --> 01:11:18.023
Forget it, okay?

01:11:18.107 --> 01:11:20.276
Your allergies are about to flare up.

01:11:21.318 --> 01:11:22.861
Isn't it a tragedy?

01:11:22.945 --> 01:11:26.031
I love cats, but I can't touch them.

01:11:27.116 --> 01:11:28.701
The cat house I made back then

01:11:30.119 --> 01:11:31.829
was the first house I ever made.

01:11:33.998 --> 01:11:35.833
I built it so poorly.

01:11:37.001 --> 01:11:39.086
But I was proud of it.

01:11:41.964 --> 01:11:44.633
I created a home
for a living thing with my own hands.

01:11:46.510 --> 01:11:47.344
I think…

01:11:49.388 --> 01:11:51.849
that's when I wanted
to become an architect.

01:11:53.142 --> 01:11:55.352
That means that cat was your first client.

01:11:55.436 --> 01:11:56.729
No.

01:11:59.106 --> 01:11:59.940
It was you.

01:12:02.359 --> 01:12:03.444
I made it for you.

01:12:04.194 --> 01:12:05.779
You were worried about the cat.

01:12:07.323 --> 01:12:08.866
I wanted you to be happy.

01:12:26.175 --> 01:12:27.301
Let's go eat.

01:12:29.345 --> 01:12:30.471
Let's go.

01:12:32.723 --> 01:12:33.932
I'm starving.

01:12:34.016 --> 01:12:36.435
Why haven't you eaten anything so late?

01:12:36.518 --> 01:12:37.811
Where should we go?

01:12:37.895 --> 01:12:39.438
My home.

01:12:43.359 --> 01:12:45.903
Your mom made a whole pot of soup
before going on the trip.

01:12:45.986 --> 01:12:48.614
It's either this or curry. Eat up.

01:12:55.037 --> 01:12:58.040
I'm sorry about before.

01:12:58.123 --> 01:13:02.169
What are you talking about?
I'm the one who caused the problem.

01:13:03.545 --> 01:13:04.463
I'm sorry.

01:13:04.546 --> 01:13:06.298
No, I was too harsh.

01:13:07.591 --> 01:13:12.888
Seeing you two together turned me
into someone petty and cheap.

01:13:13.597 --> 01:13:15.849
I'm the one who's done
more unpleasant things though.

01:13:18.602 --> 01:13:21.397
It's not great sharing
our past relationships with each other.

01:13:21.480 --> 01:13:25.317
Not knowing is one thing,
but knowing makes it hard.

01:13:25.984 --> 01:13:27.611
No wonder it's an unwritten rule.

01:13:29.279 --> 01:13:31.657
From now on,
I won't hide anything from you.

01:13:32.574 --> 01:13:34.493
I won't get involved with her
like that again.

01:13:34.576 --> 01:13:36.954
No, I won't leave any room for it.

01:13:41.959 --> 01:13:42.918
But…

01:13:44.294 --> 01:13:46.755
I was honestly happy to see you jealous.

01:13:47.506 --> 01:13:49.174
-What?
-Not a lot.

01:13:50.008 --> 01:13:51.927
Just a little bit.

01:13:56.682 --> 01:13:58.684
Still, let's not fight.

01:13:58.767 --> 01:14:01.437
It felt awful to fight with you.

01:14:02.062 --> 01:14:03.981
I couldn't focus at work,
and I was frustrated.

01:14:04.773 --> 01:14:06.024
This was a first for me.

01:14:06.900 --> 01:14:07.943
It was?

01:14:08.819 --> 01:14:09.736
Yeah.

01:14:09.820 --> 01:14:13.740
I didn't want to be someone
who was consumed by a relationship.

01:14:15.659 --> 01:14:18.078
It felt so unfamiliar.
I didn't feel like myself.

01:14:18.162 --> 01:14:21.957
Hey, that's normal.

01:14:22.040 --> 01:14:24.251
How long have you been pretending
to be cool?

01:14:24.334 --> 01:14:25.919
I don't know.

01:14:28.422 --> 01:14:29.673
I'm sure of one thing.

01:14:31.133 --> 01:14:33.635
You make me feel warm on the inside.

01:14:41.226 --> 01:14:46.482
Hey, I borrowed a lot of comic books.
They're in my room.

01:14:46.565 --> 01:14:49.443
Let's eat this quickly and read them.

01:14:50.027 --> 01:14:51.153
Yeah, sure.

01:15:04.958 --> 01:15:06.084
What are you doing?

01:15:06.168 --> 01:15:09.171
Why are you looking around
like it's your first time in here?

01:15:09.254 --> 01:15:10.756
No, it's just…

01:15:13.425 --> 01:15:17.012
Ta-da! I borrowed a whole series for you.

01:15:17.095 --> 01:15:18.597
What is this?

01:15:18.680 --> 01:15:22.309
What do you think?
It's Princess. It's your favorite.

01:15:22.392 --> 01:15:25.020
Well… Here it is. This is what I wanted.

01:15:25.854 --> 01:15:27.356
The book you wanted…

01:15:27.439 --> 01:15:29.066
was Princess?

01:15:31.693 --> 01:15:34.821
I just made that up.

01:15:34.905 --> 01:15:35.906
What?

01:15:37.324 --> 01:15:38.492
To be honest,

01:15:40.285 --> 01:15:44.081
I went to the comic book room to see you.

01:15:45.290 --> 01:15:46.542
What?

01:15:49.044 --> 01:15:50.587
Well, after being like that back then,

01:15:51.922 --> 01:15:53.423
why do you treat me this way now?

01:15:54.508 --> 01:15:55.425
What did I do?

01:15:55.509 --> 01:15:58.345
You don't seem that interested in me.

01:15:58.971 --> 01:15:59.930
Me?

01:16:00.013 --> 01:16:03.392
You can't look me in the eyes,
and you act indifferent.

01:16:04.643 --> 01:16:07.729
You treat me worse than how you did
before we started dating.

01:16:08.355 --> 01:16:13.110
Well… I mean, that's because…

01:16:13.986 --> 01:16:14.861
Well…

01:16:18.657 --> 01:16:21.451
I was just really nervous.

01:16:25.372 --> 01:16:26.832
It was because I was nervous.

01:16:47.060 --> 01:16:49.271
How can you sleep
in this kind of situation?

01:16:58.697 --> 01:17:00.949
Why am I so nervous? This is so strange.

01:17:14.963 --> 01:17:17.007
So this is what a blueprint looks like.

01:17:17.883 --> 01:17:18.717
Yeah.

01:17:23.680 --> 01:17:25.974
Really? Then I'll just buy a drink.

01:17:26.058 --> 01:17:27.059
Okay.

01:18:07.724 --> 01:18:09.351
I'd waited for so long.

01:18:11.520 --> 01:18:14.314
But when you're actually next to me…

01:18:18.652 --> 01:18:21.196
My mind goes blank,
and I don't know what to do.

01:18:25.867 --> 01:18:26.827
I thought…

01:18:27.953 --> 01:18:28.829
you were being…

01:18:30.497 --> 01:18:31.873
so calm.

01:18:34.084 --> 01:18:35.502
Now that we're dating,

01:18:36.795 --> 01:18:38.714
maybe you didn't see me as attractive.

01:18:39.673 --> 01:18:40.841
That's what I thought.

01:18:42.592 --> 01:18:45.762
I got anxious and worked up by myself.

01:18:46.388 --> 01:18:47.472
That's not it at all.

01:18:49.266 --> 01:18:50.267
It's the opposite.

01:18:55.021 --> 01:18:56.481
I like you so much.

01:18:59.609 --> 01:19:02.279
I don't know how to treat you.

01:19:18.628 --> 01:19:20.046
Let's take these downstairs.

01:19:21.631 --> 01:19:23.300
You don't want to read them here?

01:19:28.889 --> 01:19:30.307
I don't think we should stay here.

01:19:30.390 --> 01:19:31.224
Why not?

01:19:33.059 --> 01:19:34.311
I'm having bad thoughts.

01:19:35.812 --> 01:19:36.938
What bad thoughts?

01:19:40.650 --> 01:19:42.319
Thoughts I shouldn't be thinking.

01:19:44.237 --> 01:19:46.406
Cheap and crude thoughts.

01:19:47.783 --> 01:19:48.867
Unhealthy thoughts.

01:19:50.619 --> 01:19:52.454
I used to like unhealthy junk food.

01:19:56.374 --> 01:20:01.254
Powdered candy, taffy, and dalgona.

01:20:01.755 --> 01:20:06.176
-Crunch balls, corn nuts, and slushies.
-Yeah.

01:20:08.637 --> 01:20:09.763
So go ahead.

